<title>USA: USG to spend $35 mln to modernize plant.</title>
<headline>USG to spend $35 mln to modernize plant.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>USG Corp said Wednesday it plans to spend $35 million to modernize USG Interiors' Cloquet, Minn. ceiling tile plant, reducing unit manufacturing costs and increasing manufacturing capacity.</p>
<p>The project is expected to start in the fall of 1996 with anticipated completion by mid-1998.</p>
<p>One high-speed, low-cost forming machine will replace two of the oldest Auratone machines in the company.</p>
<p>USG initially purchased the Cloquet plant from Conwed Corp in 1985.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
